      "text": "Bunias orientalis, the Turkish wartycabbage, warty-cabbage, hill mustard, or Turkish rocket, is an edible wild plant species in the genus Bunias.\nIt is classified as an invasive neophyte in most of Middle Europe and parts of North America."
